# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   M. Lebeda et al. (2026). Benchmarking Universal Machine-Learning Interatomic Potentials for Temperature-Dependent Elasticity of Binary and High-Entropy Refractory Carbides.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2610.11878  arXiv:2610.11878v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2610.11878v1 (sha256 0a5893681e435acb...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 284 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/lebeda2026benchmarking.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: nine pretrained universal MLIPs (Table 1) used in
# stress-strain NPT/NVT MD of 512-atom TiC, ZrC, HfC, VC, TaC and two
# high-entropy carbides at 300-1200 K, and the stated MD speeds for a
# 512-atom TiC cell. Accuracy is reported as MAPE of elastic constants and
# moduli against AIMD and softening errors in percentage points, which are
# not energy/force/stress error metrics; no metric is encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
