###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# MD speeds for a 512-atom TiC cell (Fig. 9): SevenNet-Nano 23.4 and 30.5
# steps/s, MatterSim-v1.0.0-1M 5.9 and 7.7, ALIGNN-FF 5.2 and 7.2 on RTX
# 4090 and H100; the other six models are given only as a range (8-11.5
# and 10-16 steps/s) and are not encoded individually. Per-atom times are
# 1/(steps per second x 512). GPU memory 1.1-5.5 GiB.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The accuracy measures (MAPE of C11, C12, C44 and Hill moduli; softening errors in percentage points) are property errors with no metric type in the schema; e.g. MACE-MH-1 has the lowest overall MAPE (5.7%).
# - DPA4 and ALIGNN-FF are new registry methods (method papers not in the corpus). SevenNet and NequIP-OAM are NequIP-family models; MatterSim applies M3GNet.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/lebeda2026benchmarking.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
